&lt;p&gt;I have worked on significantly improving how Relay connects to external services and securing local data across multiple platforms. The app now feels more complete, with deeper integration capabilities for publishing content, managing notes, and running complex terminals locally.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Core Application Stability and Deployment
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The foundational structure of the application has undergone several updates. I scaffolded Relay from the Wails3 React template and upgraded to various versions of Wails and Go. This included establishing CI builds that support macOS, Windows, and Linux simultaneously. The app can now run in the background with a tray icon and proper app naming conventions across installers and bundles.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For development experience, I added features like version checking for the status page and improved release handling so that publishing happens directly from CI rather than relying on drafts. I also ensured better backward compatibility by addressing multiple system-specific bugs, such as those related to SmartScreen warnings on Windows setup or incorrect behavior in settings menus.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Content Creation and Integration
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I focused heavily on making content creation more streamlined through key integrations:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Buffer:&lt;/strong&gt; Added comprehensive support for Buffer, allowing sign-in using OAuth (Authorization Code + PKCE). I implemented a full workflow that includes the ability to create, list, edit, and draft ideas directly within Relay. Users can now see scheduled posts in a dedicated queue panel, and the composer reviews drafts before sending them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Dev.to:&lt;/strong&gt; The system can now handle publishing articles and syncing existing content with Dev.to. I also addressed how links are handled for posts that have not been published yet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Plane Kanban &amp;amp; Notes:&lt;/strong&gt; I rebuilt the Plane integration to include a full cross-project inbox, enhanced kanban boards with drag capabilities and filters, module lanes view, and item drawers that now support comments and activity tracking. Quick capture is available via &lt;code&gt;⌘K&lt;/code&gt; for immediate note saving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Local Vault and Security
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To improve data security and user experience across different operating systems, I built out the following features:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Encrypted Storage:&lt;/strong&gt; Implemented a dedicated vault using AES-256-GCM storage, which requires a keychain key for access. This ensures sensitive project and module data is locally secured.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Biometric Locking:&lt;/strong&gt; On macOS, I added functionality to lock projects and modules behind Touch ID authentication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Secrets Management:&lt;/strong&gt; I moved secrets out of plaintext configuration files (&lt;code&gt;config.toml&lt;/code&gt;) and now require them to be stored in the OS keychain or local file systems for maximum security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Advanced Terminal Capabilities
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The terminal experience received a major overhaul, providing a much more robust development environment:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Session Management:&lt;/strong&gt; I implemented Go-owned PTY sessions that support detaching and reattaching, similar to &lt;code&gt;tmux&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Enhanced UI:&lt;/strong&gt; The xterm integration now includes panes, tabs, and splits, with functionality for zooming and dragging between windows. A quick terminal view (&lt;code&gt;⌘/&lt;/code&gt;) is available over all other application views. I also added logic to detect installed shells so the app can automatically pick one on startup, even if standard shells like &lt;code&gt;zsh&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;bash&lt;/code&gt; are unavailable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  AI Providers Layer
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I introduced a dedicated provider layer in Go to manage multiple local and cloud-based generative AI services. This now supports:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Cloud Services:&lt;/strong&gt; OpenAI, Anthropic, and OpenRouter providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Local Services:&lt;/strong&gt; Automatic detection for Ollama and LM Studio local providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;  The settings section is updated to allow testing a model before saving it, and includes mechanisms to block locked data from being sent to cloud AI services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What's next&lt;br&gt;
I plan on updating the documentation with the latest changes and addressing remaining minor UI/UX touch-ups across different views.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every month I had the same problem: my money lives in three places — &lt;strong&gt;HBL&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;ABL&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;NayaPay&lt;/strong&gt; — and no single app shows the whole picture. Transfers arrive as emails, card spends arrive as SMS, and the "official" record only shows up weeks later in a PDF statement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So I built &lt;strong&gt;FinSync&lt;/strong&gt;: a personal finance engine that pulls transactions from every channel, collapses duplicates, reconciles them against bank statements, and turns it all into one clean ledger with analytics and a forecast.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;👉 &lt;strong&gt;Live demo (no signup):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://finsync-green.vercel.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://finsync-green.vercel.app&lt;/a&gt; — click &lt;strong&gt;"View live demo"&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
👉 &lt;strong&gt;Source:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/danishzulfiqar/FinSync" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/danishzulfiqar/FinSync&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fxyqhyffwq80691k2ohgl.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fxyqhyffwq80691k2ohgl.png" alt="FinSync dashboard" width="800" height="500"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


  The problem: no bank APIs in Pakistan
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the US or Europe, a budgeting app connects to your bank in two clicks through &lt;strong&gt;Plaid&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;TrueLayer&lt;/strong&gt; or a PSD2 open-banking API. In Pakistan, none of that exists for everyday users:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No public APIs.&lt;/strong&gt; Banks don't offer developer APIs to read your own account data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No aggregators.&lt;/strong&gt; There's no Plaid-style service that supports local banks, so global apps like YNAB or Mint simply can't connect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No clean exports.&lt;/strong&gt; Most banks give you a PDF statement — not a CSV — and only for past months.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So your own financial data is locked inside three separate apps, and the only things the banks &lt;em&gt;do&lt;/em&gt; hand you are the notifications they already send: &lt;strong&gt;SMS alerts, emails and PDF statements&lt;/strong&gt;. FinSync is built entirely on those — the data you already legitimately receive — without scraping banking apps, reverse-engineering private APIs or ever asking for a password or OTP.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  The real problem: one payment, three copies
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A single card payment can reach me as:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a &lt;strong&gt;real-time SMS&lt;/strong&gt; (merchant, exact time, no balance),&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a &lt;strong&gt;notification email&lt;/strong&gt; (reference number, sender name), and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;a &lt;strong&gt;statement line&lt;/strong&gt; a month later (running balance, generic description, posting date — not the transaction time).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Naively importing all three triples your spending. Naively deduplicating on amount + date merges two genuinely different ₨1,500 payments on the same day. The interesting engineering is everything in between.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  Architecture
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmermaid.ink%2Fimg%-SEJMIMK3IEFCTCDCtyBOYXlhUGF5PC9iPjxici8-QWxlcnQgZW1haWxzIl0KICAgICAgICBQREZbIjxiPkFsbCBiYW5rczwvYj48YnIvPk1vbnRobHkgUERGIHN0YXRlbWVudHMiXQogICAgICAgIEhCTF9TTVMgfn5-IEVNQUlMUyB-fn4gUERGCiAgICBlbmQKCiAgICBzdWJncmFwaCBJTkdFU1RbIjIgwrcgU2VjdXJlLCByZWFkLW9ubHkgaW5nZXN0aW9uIl0KICAgICAgICBkaXJlY3Rpb24gTFIKICAgICAgICBHQVRFV0FZWyI8Yj5BbmRyb2lkIFNNUyBHYXRld2F5PC9iPjxici8-SE1BQy1zaWduZWQgd2ViaG9vayJdCiAgICAgICAgR01BSUxbIjxiPkdtYWlsIEFQSTwvYj48YnIvPnJlYWQtb25seSBPQXV0aCJdCiAgICAgICAgVVBMT0FEWyI8Yj5TdGF0ZW1lbnQgdXBsb2FkPC9iPjxici8-cGRmcGx1bWJlciBwYXJzZXIiXQogICAgICAgIEdBVEVXQVkgfn5-IEdNQUlMIH5-fiBVUExPQUQKICAgIGVuZAoKICAgIHN1YmdyYXBoIEVOR0lORVsiMyDCtyBSZWNvbmNpbGlhdGlvbiBlbmdpbmUg4oCUIEZhc3RBUEkiXQogICAgICAgIGRpcmVjdGlvbiBMUgogICAgICAgIFBBUlNFWyI8Yj5QYXJzZTwvYj48YnIvPnBlci1iYW5rIHBhcnNlcnMiXQogICAgICAgIEZQWyI8Yj5GaW5nZXJwcmludDwvYj48YnIvPlNIQS0yNTYgaWRlbnRpdHkiXQogICAgICAgIERFRFVQKFsiPGI-RGVkdXBsaWNhdGU8L2I-PGJyLz5leGFjdCDCtyBwcm9iYWJsZSDCtyByZXZpZXciXSkKICAgICAgICBSRUNPTlsiPGI-UmVjb25jaWxlPC9iPjxici8-YWxlcnQg4oeEIHN0YXRlbWVudCJdCiAgICAgICAgQ0FUWyI8Yj5DYXRlZ29yaXplPC9iPjxici8-bGVhcm4tb25jZSBydWxlcyJdCiAgICAgICAgUEFSU0UgLS0-IEZQIC0tPiBERURVUCAtLT4gUkVDT04gLS0-IENBVAogICAgZW5kCgogICAgc3ViZ3JhcGggU1RPUkVbIjQgwrcgUG9zdGdyZVNRTCDigJQgb25lIHJvdyBwZXIgcmVhbCBldmVudCJdCiAgICAgICAgZGlyZWN0aW9uIExSCiAgICAgICAgU1JDWygiPGI--Q2FzaC1mbG93IGFuYWx5dGljczwvYj48YnIvPnRyYW5zZmVycyBleGNsdWRlZCJdCiAgICAgICAgRk9SRUNBU1RbIjxiPkJhbGFuY2UgZm9yZWNhc3Q8L2I-PGJyLz5Nb250ZS1DYXJsbyJdCiAgICAgICAgTEVER0VSIH5-fiBBTkFMWVRJQ1Mgfn5-IEZPUkVDQVNUCiAgICBlbmQKCiAgICAlJSBUaWVyLWxldmVsIGxpbmtzIGtlZXAgZWFjaCB0aWVyJ3MgbGVmdC10by1yaWdodCBsYXlvdXQgaW50YWN0LgogICAgQkFOS1MgLS0-%3D%3D%3Ftype%3Dpng%26bgColor%3D%21white%26width%3D1600" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cf